 'QNFO.INFRA; charter pillar core; roadmap row RM-TP-3-FOOTPRINT-TEARDOWN (T3 end state: archive/ holding every dead directory with a manifest). Counted 2026-11-05 ~00:30Z: 129 top-level directories, of which 36 are live workers and 64 have a wrangler.toml and a RETIRED or FOLDED marker; they still sit at the repository root, so every scan of worker directories (fleet graph, mirror-guard, version-bump-guard, worker-load-gate, the system map) walks them and every tool listing carries them. The applier half of lever 8 is done (archive/APPLIER-WORKFLOWS-MANIFEST.md, TP-3a) and its transformation_levers row reads landed, which is why this half had no owner. Work: (1) git grep RETIRED and FOLDED across scripts, .github, qnfo-fleet-control and qnfo-ops, and run fleet-graph impact on a sample of the dead workers, to list every reader that expects the marker at the root: scripts/charter-guard.py deployable_dirs(), the FOLDED-RETIRED-EXPLICIT-GUARD-1 and WORKER-RESURRECTION-GUARD-1 steps of canonical-deploy.yml, the fold-guard suites, scripts/worker_release.py, mirror-guard and the deploy-targets.txt comments; (2) make each of them read the marker from archive/<dir>/ as well (a RETIRED or FOLDED directory under archive/ must still refuse a deploy), with a test per reader; (3) generate archive/DEAD-DIRS-MANIFEST.md (directory, marker, date, successor) by a script with a --check mode and move the 64 directories with git mv in one pull request that touches no worker code; (4) keep the pull request mechanical: the dead directories have no editors, but other sessions hold claims on live ones, so run git fetch and re-check claims immediately before the move. Prediction: top-level directories 129 to about 65, no deploy of a retired worker becomes possible, worker-load-gate and the fleet graph run over 36 worker directories instead of 100. Closing marker: the change carries the text TP-3D-ARCHIVE-DEAD-DIRS-1.' || char(10) ||
